{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1137835-four-way-political-drama","id":1137835,"title":"Four way political drama?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Changeling: The Dreaming"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-09-05T14:43:55-07:00","id":1137835,"title":"Four way political drama?","content":"Has anyone ever had both the Seelie/Unseelie and Noble/Commoner divides play large roles in their games? The larps I've been involved with usually devolve into seelie = noble and unseelie = commoner, which is a bit disappointing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10243-zenten","name":"zenten","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10243_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"488"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-05T19:58:15-07:00","id":1137904,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>zenten</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1137835-four-way-political-drama#post1137835\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Has anyone ever had both the Seelie/Unseelie and Noble/Commoner divides play large roles in their games? The larps I've been involved with usually devolve into seelie = noble and unseelie = commoner, which is a bit disappointing.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> The Larp I was in had a three way push, a Gwydion Baron tried to unite the other Sidhe Barons against the &quot;Mob&quot; of Unseelie commoners. Unfortunately for him about a third of the barons were Ailil and were about as interested in letting the Gwydion take charge as eating a huge pile of shit. SO the game basically had Seelie Houses with retainer pcs. Unseelie Houses with Retainer pcs and and Unaligned Unseelie Commoners. There was no Seelie commoner camp. The Unseelie Houses got along ok with the Unseelie commoners who didn't swear to houses BUT they were clearly different factions and did have some cross issues.. They just worked together much better than the Seelie and anyone else..","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-05T23:41:05-07:00","id":1137932,"title":"","content":"In our tabletop games there was a Seelie Court, which included both Sidhe and Commoners, with a drop or two of Unseelie, Mixed Legacy Commoners, that were on the fringe or outside of direct Court's influence (who dealt with outsiders and amongst themselves case by case basis) and there were The &quot;capital letter&quot; Unseelie - marginalized and criminalized elements, either by choice or pressure, who had reasons and incentives to be actively supportive of Shadow Court... yet not necessarily were.<br /> <br /> It was more like a sliding scale, I guess. No LARP experience, though.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>...","edited":{"userid":5211,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5211-firkraag","user":"Firkraag","date":". 09-15-2017, 05:46 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5211-firkraag","n